IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spc-nouns`
IMPORT `spc-dates`
IMPORT `spc-part-interpretation`
IMPORT `spc-part-entitlement`

-- State Pension Credit Act 2002 -- LAYER 1, Schedule 2 (Minor and consequential
-- amendments).
--
-- Schedule 2 amends other Acts so that state pension credit sits alongside the
-- benefits they already deal with. Almost every paragraph inserts the words "state
-- pension credit" into a list in another Act, or substitutes it for "income support"
-- in a provision whose full text is not in this Act. What a deposited paragraph
-- says is the AMENDMENT, not the amended provision, so the effect of most of them
-- on a person cannot be stated from this text and they are inert, each with its
-- reason. Five paragraphs insert a free-standing provision whose operative words ARE
-- here, and those are encoded: paragraph 2 (conditions of entitlement to income
-- support), paragraph 4 (the definition of the qualifying age), paragraph 17
-- (section 159B of the Administration Act), paragraph 26 (Transport Act 1982),
-- paragraph 30 (Children Act 1989).
--
-- Each encoded rule states the provision AS INSERTED. Whether the section it was
-- inserted into still reads that way today is a question about that other Act, which
-- is not among the inputs (fork F-18, NOTES.md).

§ `Schedule 2 -- Minor and consequential amendments`

§§ `Part 1 -- Amendments of the Contributions and Benefits Act`

-- Paragraph 2(2), (3): section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act, on
-- entitlement to income support, gains (aa) "he has not attained the qualifying age
-- for state pension credit" and (g) "if he is a member of a married or unmarried
-- couple, the other member of the couple is not entitled to state pension credit".
-- Both are conditions of entitlement to income support, not to state pension
-- credit. "Married or unmarried couple" has the meaning that Act gives it, which is
-- not among the inputs, so whether the claimant is a member of one is a fact.
-- src:451 | (2) In subsection (1) (entitlement to income support), after paragraph (a) (claimant must be 16 or over) insert—
-- src:452 | (aa) he has not attained the qualifying age for state pension credit;
-- src:453 | (3) In that subsection, after paragraph (f) (claimant must not be entitled to jobseeker’s allowance etc) insert
-- src:454 | ; and
-- src:455 | (g) if he is a member of a married or unmarried couple, the other member of the couple is not entitled to state pension credit.
@ref Sch 2 para 2(2), (3) (inserting s 124(1)(aa) and (g) of the Contributions and Benefits Act) (src:451-455)
GIVEN case IS A Case
      `the claimant is a member of a married or unmarried couple` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 2 -- the conditions inserted into section 124(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act are met` case `the claimant is a member of a married or unmarried couple` MEANS
        "(aa) he has not attained the qualifying age for state pension credit;" ... NOT (`s 1(6) -- has attained the qualifying age on` (case's `day tested`) (case's claimant))
    AND "(g) if he is a member of a married or unmarried couple, the other member of the couple is not entitled to state pension credit." ... (    NOT `the claimant is a member of a married or unmarried couple`
                                                                                                                                                  OR NOT (case's `other member entitled to state pension credit`) )

-- Paragraph 3: inserts section 136A into the Contributions and Benefits Act. Its
-- subsections are powers to make regulations about housing benefit and council tax
-- benefit for a person who has attained the qualifying age for state pension credit
-- (so that the ordinary rules need not apply, and income and capital are determined as
-- for state pension credit), and a power to apply section 12 (polygamous marriages).
-- Nothing is decided for a person without those regulations.
-- Paragraph 1 introduces the Part. Paragraph 5 amends section 148 (Christmas bonus):
-- substitutes "state pension credit" for "income support" in subsection (2)(c)(ii),
-- inserts subsection (2A) (reading "pensionable age" as the qualifying age for state
-- pension credit) and omits subsection (4). Paragraph 6 amends section 149
-- (Christmas bonus: supplementary) by substituting "state pension credit" for "income
-- support". Paragraph 7 amends section 150 (interpretation of the Christmas bonus
-- provisions) by the same substitution and repeats the definitions of the qualifying
-- age and of state pension credit. Section 148 to 150 are not in this text, so the
-- conditions of the Christmas bonus cannot be stated from it.

-- Paragraph 4 inserts into section 137(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act the
-- definition of "the qualifying age for state pension credit": for a woman,
-- pensionable age; for a man, the age which is pensionable age for a woman born on the
-- same day as the man. It repeats section 1(6) of this Act (which it cites), so the
-- rule delegates to it and states the relation once (spc-part-entitlement.l4).
-- src:475 | “pensionable age” has the meaning given by the rules in paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995 (c. 26);
-- src:476 | “the qualifying age for state pension credit” is (in accordance with section 1(2)(b) and (6) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002)—
-- src:477 | (a) in the case of a woman, pensionable age; or
-- src:478 | (b) in the case of a man, the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day as the man;
-- src:479 | “state pension credit” means state pension credit under the State Pension Credit Act 2002;
@ref Sch 2 para 4 (inserting definitions into s 137(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act) (src:475-479)
GIVEN person IS A Person
GIVETH A DATE
`Sch 2 para 4 -- the day the person attains the qualifying age for state pension credit` person MEANS
    `s 1(6) -- the day the person attains the qualifying age` person

§§ `Part 2 -- Amendments of the Administration Act`

-- Paragraphs 8 and 9: paragraph 8 introduces the Part; paragraph 9 is blank in the
-- deposited text (a row of dots) and is treated as repealed or blank.
-- Paragraph 10 adds state pension credit to the benefits in section 71(11)
-- (overpayments of benefit). Paragraph 11 adds it to section 74(1)(b) and (2)(b)
-- (recovery of income support etc paid because of late payment of income or of
-- public funds). Paragraph 12 adds this Act to the "relevant social security
-- legislation" in section 121DA(1) (enforcement). Paragraph 13 adds it to the
-- provisions about information from registers of births, marriages and deaths
-- (section 124(1)); paragraph 14 to the regulations about notification of death
-- (section 125(1)); paragraph 15 to the duty of personal representatives to furnish
-- information about the estate of a person in receipt of certain benefits (section
-- 126(1)). Paragraph 16 adds the sums specified in regulations under section 2 or
-- 3 of this Act to those the Secretary of State reviews for annual up-rating (section
-- 150(1)) and this Act to section 150(7). Each is a list insertion in another Act.

-- Paragraph 17 inserts section 159B into the Administration Act: effect of alterations
-- affecting state pension credit. It applies, subject to prescribed exceptions and
-- conditions, where an award of state pension credit is in force and an alteration in
-- (i) a component of state pension credit, (ii) the recipient's benefit income, (iii) a
-- component of contribution-based jobseeker's allowance, or (iv) the recipient's war
-- disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension affects the computation of
-- the amount of state pension credit to which the recipient is entitled. Then, as
-- from the commencing date, the amount payable is the increased or reduced amount
-- without any further decision (subsection (2)), or the award continues if the same
-- amount is still due (subsection (3)). It duplicates section 10 of this Act for a wider
-- set of alterations, so it is a separate rule (the trigger differs), with the same
-- shape: where section 159B does not apply the answer is NOTHING (the paragraph says
-- nothing about what is payable then), and before the commencing date the existing
-- award's amount (an input) is returned, as for section 10 (fork F-23).
-- src:529 | (1) Subject to such exceptions and conditions as may be prescribed, subsection (2) or (3) below shall have effect where—
-- src:530 | (a) an award of state pension credit is in force in favour of any person (“the recipient”); and
-- src:531 | (b) an alteration—
-- src:532 | (i) in any component of state pension credit,
-- src:533 | (ii) in the recipient’s benefit income,
-- src:534 | (iii) in any component of a contribution-based jobseeker’s allowance, or
-- src:535 | (iv) in the recipient’s war disablement pension or war widow’s or widower’s pension,
-- src:536 | affects the computation of the amount of state pension credit to which he is entitled.
-- src:537 | (2) Where, as a result of the alteration, the amount of state pension credit to which the recipient is entitled is increased or reduced, then, as from the commencing date, the amount of state pension credit payable in the case of the recipient under the award shall be the increased or reduced amount, without any further decision of the Secretary of State; and the award shall have effect accordingly.
-- src:538 | (3) Where, notwithstanding the alteration, the recipient continues on and after the commencing date to be entitled to the same amount of state pension credit as before, the award shall continue in force accordingly.
@ref Sch 2 para 17 (inserting s 159B(1) to (3) of the Administration Act) (src:529-538)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the commencing date` IS A DATE
      `an award of state pension credit is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an alteration in a component of state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an alteration in the recipient's benefit income` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an alteration in a component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an alteration in the recipient's war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration affects the computation of the amount of state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a prescribed exception or condition takes the case outside section 159B` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount payable before the commencing date` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount to which the recipient is entitled after the alteration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Sch 2 para 17 -- the amount of state pension credit payable on` day `under section 159B given the commencing date` `the commencing date` `with an award in force` `an award of state pension credit is in force` `and an alteration in a component` `there is an alteration in a component of state pension credit` `or in benefit income` `there is an alteration in the recipient's benefit income` `or in a jobseeker's allowance component` `there is an alteration in a component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` `or in a war pension` `there is an alteration in the recipient's war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` `that affects the computation` `the alteration affects the computation of the amount of state pension credit` `outside any prescribed exception` `a prescribed exception or condition takes the case outside section 159B` `from the amount before` `the amount payable before the commencing date` `to the amount after` `the amount to which the recipient is entitled after the alteration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (   "(a) an award of state pension credit is in force in favour of any person (\"the recipient\"); and" ... `an award of state pension credit is in force`
           AND "(b) an alteration (i) in any component of state pension credit, (ii) in the recipient's benefit income, (iii) in any component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance, or (iv) in the recipient's war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension," ...
                   (       `there is an alteration in a component of state pension credit`
                       OR  `there is an alteration in the recipient's benefit income`
                       OR  `there is an alteration in a component of a contribution-based jobseeker's allowance`
                       OR  `there is an alteration in the recipient's war disablement pension or war widow's or widower's pension` )
           AND `the alteration affects the computation of the amount of state pension credit`
           AND NOT `a prescribed exception or condition takes the case outside section 159B` )
        THEN NOTHING
        IF day AT LEAST `the commencing date`
        THEN JUST `the amount to which the recipient is entitled after the alteration`
        OTHERWISE JUST `the amount payable before the commencing date`

-- Paragraph 17 also inserts section 159B(4) to (6): when a statement is made in the House
-- of Commons proposing an alteration, an award made after it and before the proposed
-- commencing date may be paid from that date at a rate set by the proposed amounts, or
-- may be expressed in the amounts in force at the date of the award; and the
-- definitions ("alteration", "benefit income", "the commencing date", "component",
-- "war disablement pension", "war widow's or widower's pension"). Subsection (5) says
-- an award "may" take either form, which is the Secretary of State's choice and
-- creates no test on a claimant's facts; the definitions repeat section 17(1) of this
-- Act and the references in section 159B(1).
-- src:539 | (4) Subsection (5) below applies where a statement is made in the House of Commons by or on behalf of the Secretary of State which specifies—
-- src:540 | (a) in relation to any of the items referred to in subsection (1)(b)(i) to (iv) above, the amount of the alteration which he proposes to make by an order under section 150 or 152 above or by or under any other enactment; and
-- src:541 | (b) the date on which he proposes to bring the alteration into force (“the proposed commencing date”).
-- src:542 | (5) If, in a case where this subsection applies, an award of state pension credit is made in favour of a person before the proposed commencing date and after the date on which the statement is made, the award—
-- src:543 | (a) may provide for state pension credit to be paid as from the proposed commencing date at a rate determined by reference to the amounts of the items specified in subsection (1)(b)(i) to (iv) above which will be in force on that date; or
-- src:544 | (b) may be expressed in terms of the amounts of those items in force at the date of the award.
-- src:545 | (6) In this section—
-- src:546 | “alteration” means—
-- src:547 | (a) in relation to any component of state pension credit, its alteration by or under any enactment;
-- src:548 | (b) in relation to a person’s benefit income, the alteration of any of the sums referred to in section 150 above by any enactment or by an order under section 150 or 152 above to the extent that any such alteration affects the amount of his benefit income;
-- src:549 | (c) in relation to any component of a contribution-based jobseeker’s allowance, its alteration by or under any enactment; and
-- src:550 | (d) in relation to a person’s war disablement pension or war widow’s or widower’s pension, its alteration by or under any enactment;
-- src:551 | “benefit income”, in relation to a person, means so much of his income as consists of benefit under the Contributions and Benefits Act;
-- src:552 | “the commencing date”, in relation to an alteration, means the date on which the alteration comes into force in relation to the recipient;
-- src:553 | “component”—
-- src:554 | (a) in relation to contribution-based jobseeker’s allowance, means any of the sums specified in regulations under the Jobseekers Act 1995 (c. 18) which are relevant in calculating the amount payable by way of a jobseeker’s allowance;
-- src:555 | (b) in relation to state pension credit, means any of the sums specified in regulations under section 2, 3 or 12 of the State Pension Credit Act 2002;
-- src:556 | “war disablement pension” means—
-- src:557 | (a) any retired pay, pension or allowance granted in respect of disablement under powers conferred by or under—
-- src:558 | (i) the Air Force (Constitution) Act 1917 (c. 51);
-- src:559 | (ii) the Personal Injuries (Emergency Provisions) Act 1939 (c. 82);
-- src:560 | (iii) the Pensions (Navy, Army, Air Force and Mercantile Marine) Act 1939 (c. 83);
-- src:561 | (iv) the Polish Resettlement Act 1947 (c. 19); or
-- src:562 | (v) Part 7 or section 151 of the Reserve Forces Act 1980 (c. 9); or
-- src:563 | (b) without prejudice to paragraph (a), any retired pay or pension to which subsection (1) of section 315 of the Income and Corporation Taxes Act 1988 (c. 1) applies;
-- src:564 | “war widow’s or widower’s pension” means—
-- src:565 | (a) any widow’s or widower’s pension or allowance granted in respect of a death due to service or war injury and payable by virtue of any enactment mentioned in paragraph (a) of the definition of “war disablement pension”; or
-- src:566 | (b) a pension or allowance for a widow or widower granted under any scheme mentioned in section 315(2)(e) of the Income and Corporation Taxes Act 1988.
-- (not encoded: section 159B(4) to (6) allow a choice of the form of an award and repeat definitions)

-- Paragraph 18: adjustments between the National Insurance Fund and the Consolidated
-- Fund (section 165): expenses of state pension credit are excluded from an estimate.
-- Paragraph 19: adds this Act to section 169(1) (adjustments of the social fund,
-- Consolidated Fund and National Insurance Fund). Paragraph 20: adds this Act to the
-- "relevant enactments" for the Social Security Advisory Committee (section 170(5)).
-- Paragraph 21: adds this Act to the reciprocal agreements provisions (section 179).
-- Paragraph 22: adds this Act to the travelling expenses provisions (section 180).
-- Paragraph 23: makes state pension credit inalienable (section 187(1)). Paragraph 24:
-- adds state pension credit to "benefit" and defines "state pension credit" (section 191).
-- Paragraph 23 adds state pension credit to a list in section 187(1), whose heading in
-- the deposited text is "Certain benefits to be inalienable"; the rule that section states
-- is in section 187, which is not in this text, so it is not encoded.

§§ `Part 3 -- Amendments of other Acts`

-- Paragraph 25 is blank in the deposited text (a row of dots).

-- Paragraph 26 inserts (bb) into section 70(2) of the Transport Act 1982: payments by
-- the Secretary of State in respect of applicants for medical exemption from wearing
-- seat belts are made for "those in receipt of guarantee state pension credit (under
-- section 1(3)(a) ...) and those persons who (within the meaning of that Act) are
-- members of a married or unmarried couple the other member of which is in receipt
-- of guarantee state pension credit". Being "in receipt" is having it paid, which is
-- not the same as being entitled (an entitlement that is not payable is not receipt),
-- so each member's receipt is a fact. "Couple" has this Act's meaning (section 17(1)).
-- src:604 | In section 70(2) of the Transport Act 1982 (c. 49) (payments by Secretary of State in respect of applicants for medical exemption from wearing seat belts) after paragraph (b), insert—
-- src:605 | (bb) those in receipt of guarantee state pension credit (under section 1(3)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002) and those persons who (within the meaning of that Act) are members of a married or unmarried couple the other member of which is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit;
@ref Sch 2 para 26 (inserting s 70(2)(bb) of the Transport Act 1982) (src:604-605)
GIVEN household IS A Household
      `the person is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 26 -- the Secretary of State makes the payment under section 70(2) of the Transport Act 1982 for` household `the person is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` `the other member of the couple is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` MEANS
        "(bb) those in receipt of guarantee state pension credit (under section 1(3)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002)" ... `the person is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit`
    OR  "and those persons who (within the meaning of that Act) are members of a married or unmarried couple the other member of which is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit;" ... (    `s 17(1) -- couple` household
                                                                                                                                                                                                       AND `the other member of the couple is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` )

-- Paragraphs 27 and 29: community charge. Paragraph 27 (Abolition of Domestic Rates
-- Etc. (Scotland) Act 1987, Schedule 2) and paragraph 29 (Local Government Finance Act
-- 1988, Schedule 4) each insert "This paragraph applies to state pension credit as it
-- applies to income support" into a paragraph about deductions from income support for
-- unpaid community charge that continues to have effect only so far as a 1993 Saving
-- Order preserves it. What the deductions are is in the amended paragraphs, which are
-- not in this text.
-- Paragraph 28 is blank (a row of dots).

-- Paragraph 30 inserts section 29(3B) into the Children Act 1989: no person is liable
-- to pay a charge under section 29(1) for a service provided under section 18(2) or (6)
-- at any time when (a) he is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit under section
-- 1(3)(a), or (b) he is a member of a married or unmarried couple (within the meaning
-- of that Act) the other member of which is in receipt of guarantee state pension
-- credit. A liability that is removed, so the rule answers whether the person is free
-- of the charge. The scope of "a service provided under section 18(2) or (6)" is the
-- Children Act's, not asked here: the question is about the charge.
-- src:615 | In section 29 of the Children Act 1989 (c. 41) (recoupment of cost of providing day care and other services) after subsection (3A) (no charge for certain services if receiving income support or income-based jobseeker’s allowance) insert—
-- src:616 | (3B) No person shall be liable to pay any charge under subsection (1) for a service provided under section 18(2) or (6) at any time when—
-- src:617 | (a) he is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit under section 1(3)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002, or
-- src:618 | (b) he is a member of a married or unmarried couple (within the meaning of that Act) the other member of which is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit.
@ref Sch 2 para 30 (inserting s 29(3B) of the Children Act 1989) (src:615-618)
GIVEN household IS A Household
      `the person is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other member of the couple is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 2 para 30 -- the person is not liable to pay a charge under section 29(1) of the Children Act 1989 for a service under section 18(2) or (6) when` household `the person is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` `the other member of the couple is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` MEANS
        "(a) he is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit under section 1(3)(a) of the State Pension Credit Act 2002, or" ... `the person is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit`
    OR  "(b) he is a member of a married or unmarried couple (within the meaning of that Act) the other member of which is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit." ... (    `s 17(1) -- couple` household
                                                                                                                                                                                  AND `the other member of the couple is in receipt of guarantee state pension credit` )

-- Paragraph 31 amends section 24 of the Criminal Justice Act 1991 (recovery of fines
-- by deduction from income support and jobseeker's allowance), substituting "a
-- jobseeker's allowance or state pension credit" in two places. Paragraphs 32 to 35
-- make the same substitution in Schedule 4 and Schedule 8 of the Local Government
-- Finance Act 1992 (deductions from benefit for unpaid council tax) and, in paragraph
-- 34, add "deductions from state pension credit may be resorted to more than once".
-- The deductions, and the limits on them, are in the amended provisions, not here.

-- Paragraphs 36 to 38 (Jobseekers Act 1995) are repealed in the deposited text
-- (rendered as {repealed: ...}); they are treated as repealed.

-- Paragraph 39 amends paragraph 1 of Schedule 4 to the Pensions Act 1995 so that the
-- rules for pensionable age apply for the purposes of this Act. That is the source of
-- the definition of "pensionable age" that section 17(1) of this Act cites; the rules
-- themselves are in the Pensions Act and are not among the inputs (the two days at which
-- pensionable age is attained are facts in the Person record).

-- Paragraphs 40 and 41 amend section 34(3) of the Social Security Act 1998 (priority
-- for housing benefit and council tax benefit claims) by adding "or state pension
-- credit". Paragraph 42 is blank. Paragraph 43 adds state pension credit to section 94
-- of the Local Government Act 2000 (disclosure of information).
-- Paragraphs 44 to 49 amend the Social Security Fraud Act 2001: paragraph 45 inserts
-- section 7(4A) (regulations may provide that where the sanctionable benefit is state
-- pension credit it is payable as if its rate were reduced in a prescribed manner during
-- a loss-of-benefit period), paragraph 46 inserts section 9(4A) for the offender's
-- family, paragraph 47 adds this Act to section 10(3), paragraph 48 adds references to
-- subsections (4A) to the draft-regulations requirement in section 11(3), paragraph 49
-- defines "state pension credit". These are powers to make regulations whose content
-- is not among the inputs, and list insertions.
